{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Qar6VZSWCT57TuyWHJ3hc","type":"tool_result","content":"331\talmanac_harden_reviewer_prompt() {\n332\t  local target=\"$1\"\n333\t  local lens=\"${2:-correctness}\"\n334\t  local rubric_path=\"${3:-}\"\n335\t  local directive=\"${4:-}\"\n336\t  local rubric_bar=\"\"\n337\t\n338\t  if [ -n \"$rubric_path\" ] && [ -f \"$rubric_path\" ]; then\n339\t    rubric_bar=\"$(almanac_harden_rubric_acceptance \"$rubric_path\")\"\n340\t  fi\n341\t\n342\t  cat <<EOF\n343\tYou are a read-only code reviewer. Lens: ${lens}.\n344\t\n345\tReview the target below for ${lens} defects only. You cannot modify any files;\n346\tthis is a read-only review.\n347\t\n348\tTarget: ${target}\n349\tEOF\n350\t\n351\t  if [ -n \"$rubric_bar\" ]; then\n352\t    cat <<EOF\n353\t\n354\tJudge the target against this acceptance bar (the rubric contract). A finding is\n355\tonly blocking if it violates a criterion below or demonstrably breaks behavior:\n356\t\n357\t${rubric_bar}\n358\tEOF\n359\t  fi\n360\t\n361\t  if [ -n \"$directive\" ]; then\n362\t    cat <<EOF\n363\t\n364\tThe operator steered this run with the directive below — follow it and prioritize\n365\tthe findings it points you toward:\n366\t\n367\t${directive}\n368\tEOF\n369\t  fi\n370\t\n371\t  cat <<EOF\n372\t\n373\tReport each defect as one JSON object per line (JSON Lines) and output nothing\n374\telse — no prose, no markdown fences. Each object must use this schema:\n375\t\n376\t{\"lens\":\"${lens}\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"location\":\"<file:line or symbol>\",\"claim\":\"<one-line defect>\",\"demonstration\":\"<failing test, breaking input, or cited rubric criterion>\"}\n377\t\n378\tOnly report a defect you can demonstrate with a failing test, a specific breaking\n379\tinput, or a cited criterion. If you find no demonstrable defects, output nothing.\n380\tEOF\n381\t}\n382\t\n383\t# Normalize the reviewer's JSON-Lines result into TSV rows\n384\t# (lens, severity, location, claim, demonstration). Malformed lines are dropped\n385\t# cleanly. Prefers jq; falls back to a flat-field awk extractor when jq is absent\n386\t# so harden keeps almanac's near-zero-dependency promise.\n387\talmanac_harden_findings_tsv() {\n388\t  local result_file=\"$1\"\n389\t\n390\t  [ -f \"$result_file\" ] || return 0\n391\t\n392\t  if command -v jq >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n393\t    jq -Rr '\n394\t      fromjson?\n395\t      | select(type == \"object\")\n396\t      | {\n397\t          lens: (.lens // \"\"),\n398\t          severity: (.severity // \"\"),\n399\t          location: (.location // \"\"),\n400\t          claim: (.claim // \"\"),\n401\t          demonstration: (.demonstration // \"\")\n402\t        }\n403\t      | select(\n404\t          (.lens | type == \"string\" and length > 0) and\n405\t          (.severity | type == \"string\" and length > 0) and\n406\t          (.location | type == \"string\" and length > 0) and\n407\t          (.claim | type == \"string\" and length > 0) and\n408\t          (.demonstration | type == \"string\" and length > 0)\n409\t        )\n410\t      | [.lens, .severity, .location, .claim, .demonstration]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FJ9EEdfdtbtg8quvqZtx5v","session_id":"2b01beec-8e7f-499f-84c4-979f364c4a47","uuid":"ad690598-2321-4923-9e6a-dff887b8f176","timestamp":"2026-05-27T06:22:23.226Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Codebase architectural friction survey"}
